            <ArticleTitle>Spondyloarthropathies: using presentation to make the diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>184-5, 189, 192-4 passim</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diagnosing the spondyloarthropathies--chronic inflammatory diseases of the spine and peripheral joints that share several distinctive features--is challenging and depends on careful evaluation of the history, physical examination, and radiographs. The recent use of tumor necrosis factor inhibitors is exciting and may represent true disease-modifying drugs for these conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
